[3] min rho_j (parity floor) vs the original R-14Q floor magnitude:
   parity-descent rho floor (min over all levels/samples) = 0.6659
   => meas(lonely S) >= (min rho)^depth . PROD caps  -- positive if rho floor>0
   depths<= 6, so worst product factor (min rho)^6 = 8.7188e-02

======================================================================================
If min rho_j > 0 uniformly and meas(lonely O_j)>0 (odd caps), the 2-adic
parity descent PROVES the covering floor recursively.  The 2-sheet CV bound
is the clean per-level certificate (2 sheets, not 14).
